        "title": "GPT-6.1 Terra fast-tier routing constants",
        "summary": "The shared model catalog in `common` adds `FREEBUFF_GPT_61_TERRA_FAST_UPSTREAM_ORDER` and `FREEBUFF_GPT_61_TERRA_FAST_MAX_PRICE` to support the first-thread A/B experiment for GPT-6.1 Terra. The routing order prioritizes OpenAI's `openai/fast` endpoint with the standard tier as a backup, ensuring a capacity refusal results in a slower turn rather than a failure. The price ceiling is set to $2.50/$12.50 per million tokens to strictly exceed the fast tier's $2/$10 card while remaining below any higher bands.",
